Subject: [PATCH] net: HTTP/3 through a SOCKS5 proxy

With a single-hop SOCKS5 proxy, QUIC runs over a SOCKS5 UDP association,
so HTTP/3 works through the proxy. HTTP, HTTPS, SOCKS4 and multi-proxy
chains refuse QUIC, since they cannot carry datagrams. HTTP/3 is reached
through Alt-Svc only, because an HTTPS DNS record lookup for the
destination would go around the proxy. Every QUIC socket, including
migration and port probes, goes through the relay, and packet size and
ECN account for the relay so QUIC sees no path-MTU black hole.

